From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:25:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [voicecall] Support building against Qt 6.

The sources build against Qt 5 or Qt 6 from the same tree:

  - qofono and mlite are looked up as qofono-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION} and
    mlite$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION} rather than hardcoding their Qt 5 flavours.
  - qt5-boostable is only looked for on Qt 5; there is no Qt 6 equivalent
    and packagesExist() would warn on every build otherwise.
  - The commhistory and filter plugins are only built when commhistory-qt
    is installed. They are optional, and commhistory-qt is part of the
    Nemo stack and not available everywhere.
  - The recorder uses the Qt 6 multimedia API - QAudioSource,
    QAudioDevice and QMediaDevices - behind QT_VERSION checks. Qt 6
    dropped setSampleSize/setCodec/setByteOrder/setSampleType: a
    QAudioFormat there is always host-order linear PCM described by a
    single sample format, so Int16 replaces the four Qt 5 calls, and
    preferredFormat() replaces nearestFormat().
  - Q_MOC_INCLUDE tells moc where forward-declared types used in
    properties live; it needs Qt 5.15 or newer, so it is guarded.
  - QString::SkipEmptyParts moved to Qt::SkipEmptyParts in Qt 5.14 and is
    gone in Qt 6, so the cell broadcast code uses the latter there.
  - Qt 6 removed QGeoPositionInfoSource::updateTimeout(); a timed out
    update is reported as errorOccurred(UpdateTimeoutError) instead, so
    the geofence listens for that on Qt 6.
  - The cell broadcast store test runs with QTEST_GUILESS_MAIN. On Qt 6
    QSqlDatabase needs a QCoreApplication to load its driver ("QSqlDatabase
    requires a QCoreApplication"), and without one the test crashed in
    QSqlDatabase::open().

Also lets a distribution point the plugin directory somewhere other than
$$[QT_INSTALL_LIBS] via VOICECALL_INSTALL_LIBDIR, since that value comes
from the Qt running qmake, which is the host Qt when cross-building.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/sailfishos/voicecall/pull/29]
